# @hsk-sync:note-meta

Token `@hsk-sync:note-meta` marks shared **note title / note date** resolution used when the UI or site does not use the raw file name alone.

If priority, parsing rules, or date formats change in any implementation, update the others and consider how lists, tabs, generated HTML titles/dates, and Vector Icons catalog titles will look.

## Sibling implementations

| Block | Path |
|-------|------|
| Python (this repo, source of truth) | `src/harrix_pylib/note_meta.py` |
| Python (pyssg re-export) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-pyssg\src\harrix_pyssg\note_meta.py` |
| VS Code (JS) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-swiss-knife\vscode\harrix-notes-explorer-hsk\note-meta.js` |
| Android (Kotlin) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-notes-android` — `NoteMetaResolver.kt`, `NoteTitleExtractor.kt` |

## Shared contract

### Title (`resolve_note_title` / `resolveTitle`)

1. YAML frontmatter `title:` (quoted/unquoted scalar).
2. Else first Markdown `#` heading (skip fenced code and HTML comment lines).
3. Else `title_from_id(file_stem)`: part after first `__`, `-`/`_` → spaces, `str.title()`.
4. Else `Untitled`.

### Date (`resolve_note_date` / `resolveDate`)

1. First date fragment in the file name / stem: `YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYY.MM.DD`, `YYYYMMDD`, or `DD.MM.YYYY`.
2. Else YAML frontmatter `date:`.
3. Else file creation time (birthtime/ctime when available).
4. Else file modification time (mtime).

Return both the calendar date and a source tag (`filename` / `yaml` / `file_ctime` / `file_mtime`) so UIs can format date-only vs date-time.

## Change checklist

- Keep regexes / priority identical across Python, JS, and Kotlin.
- Update unit tests in `tests/test_note_meta.py` when behavior changes.
- After pylib changes, run linked `hsk py ruff-sort-docs` + `hsk py check` on swiss-knife, pylib, and pyssg.
